Z||000000||doughboySE||08-08-2000||09:34 PM||||GT BASTARD HEHE I KNOW I SPELLED THAT WRONG <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>ok here is my question. i have noticed lately that when i step on the gas to take off or get going faster, that the car seems to want to bog a bit before getting going.<BR>its almost as if it wants to stall but it dosnt stall . it just dosnt seem to have the power i thought it used to in the bottom end.<BR>any suggestions would greatly be helped||||reg||1
Z||000001||RobertVol||08-08-2000||10:49 PM||||I have been having the same problem with mine. Once I hit the gas after dropping the clutch It LURCHES forward and bucks a little and then evens out and goes. But its real iritating. I have checked most of the obvious things but cant seem to find the problem. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||fropuff||08-09-2000||12:26 PM||||I had the exact problem.  But, I figured it out when my dad and I went on a long trip.  The trips I take now are between 1 and 1.5 miles to the paint guys' house.  The idle was erratic and the acceleration from a stop was crappy.  When I took a ten mile trip, this got a little better.  I'm going to take a lot longer trip when I'm done with the paint job.  Hope this helps.  Also, my problems got better when I went the same speed (about 50.) ||||reg||1
Z||000003||btoth||08-09-2000||12:44 PM||||mine bogged down really bad whenever i would try to accellerate until i replaced my catalytic converter... now it runs great.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Jim's87GT||08-09-2000||03:48 PM||||The problem I had was caused by a clogged Cat.  I couldn't get the U-Bolts off of the Cat so I removed the EGR to see if more flow would help.  (At that time the engine wouldn't go over 2,700 RPM)  With the EGR off it IDLED at 4,500 RPM!  New Cat - No problems.||||reg||1
Z||000005||286SE'S||08-09-2000||04:18 PM||||I was just having some problems accelerating, kind of a stumble when I let off the clutch. <BR>Replaced the easy stuff, plugs, wires, cap and rotor. Seems to have take care of it but its only been a few days. My pickup coil looks really crappy and that will be next, just because it looks original. My cat died at about 90,000 miles,(two years ago) it ran really great for about 2 weeks and I felt like I had a new car then it just went back to its usual good-day bad-day as far as performance (its a 4 cyl) Usually washing it and giving it a nice polish increases the good-days.<BR>Terry||||reg||1
